  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-506696</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective (OO/Impact): Women, in all their diversity , influence decision-making processes on climate change and environmental conservation policies and actions in Viet Nam.
Specific Objective (SO/Outcome): Improved access to decent jobs andentrepreneurship opportunities in the green economy and the circular economy for women in all their diversity .
The two outputs (OP) below aredesigned to contribute to the Specific Objective
Output 1: Strengthened technical, operational, and networkingcapacities of gender-responsive and environmentally sensitive NSAs to implement initiatives in the field of climate change adaptation and mitigation, disaster risk reduction, environmental protection, sustainable agriculture, sustainable forestry, responsible consumption and production practices, and gender equality.
Output 2: Increased public and private sector financing mechanisms for MSMEs, owned or managed by women, including women&#x2019;s informal business gender bonds.
Three Sub-Outputs (SOP) are designed to contribute to the achievement of these two Outputs and to also contribute to four Outputs under SO1 of the CfP.
Sub-output 1: Approximately 65 sub-grants (ranging from&#x20ac;50,000 to &#x20ac;60,000 per grant), relating to eight Green Deal priorities and threeGender Action Plan III priorities will be successfully implemented to improve climate change adaptation and mitigation, environmental protection, disaster risk reduction, access to decent jobs and entrepreneurship opportunities for women and girls in alltheir diversity in the green and circular economy.
Sub-output2: Improvement of technical knowledge, operations, networking, and contribution to decision-making processes of at least 65 organizations, with at least 325 individuals , on gender equalityand gender-responsive climate change adaptation and mitigation, disaster risk reduction, environmental protection, sustainable agriculture and forestry, responsible consumption, and production practices.
Sub-output 3: Multi-stakeholder partnerships betweenatleast 65 organizations and linkages with the TA Facility will be established forsharing expertise, experience, knowledge, and effective participation in policy dialogue to promote a gender-responsive green transition.</narrative>
  </description>
